cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, these protocols, or this code, please cite the paper below."
title: "Candidate Presentation Instability in LLM Answer Verification"
abstract: >-
  A label-symmetric benchmark of 10,500 items and six controlled verification
  protocols for measuring how far a large language model's correctness verdict
  moves under label-preserving changes in how a candidate answer is presented,
  reported against a same-prompt repeat baseline, responsiveness, and output
  coverage.
type: software
